<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Getting Started on iOS UIKit Course</title><link>/docs/01-getting-started/getting-started/</link><description>Recent content in Getting Started on iOS UIKit Course</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="/docs/01-getting-started/getting-started/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title/><link>/docs/01-getting-started/getting-started/preparing-your-development-environment/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/01-getting-started/getting-started/preparing-your-development-environment/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="preparing-your-development-environment"&gt;Preparing your Development Environment&lt;a class="anchor" href="#preparing-your-development-environment"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3 id="you-cannot-build-native-ios-apps-in-windows-or-linux-oss"&gt;&lt;mark style="color:red;"&gt;You cannot build native iOS apps in Windows or Linux OSs.&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#you-cannot-build-native-ios-apps-in-windows-or-linux-oss"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3 id="i-recommend-using-a-macbook-or-an-apple-computer-for-this-course-you-do-not-need-an-iphoneipad-for-this-course-if-you-do-not-have-a-macbook-you-can-try-macincloud-or-even-try-borrowing-macbooks-from-the-library-i-am-not-sure-how-long-you-can-borrow-a-computer-from-there-you-can-even-talk-to-khoury-systems-to-check-if-they-lend-macbooks-for-a-semester"&gt;&lt;mark style="color:red;"&gt;I recommend using a Macbook or an Apple Computer for this course. You do not need an iPhone/iPad for this course. If you do not have a Macbook, you can try MacInCloud, or even try borrowing Macbooks from the library (I am not sure how long you can borrow a computer from there). You can even talk to Khoury Systems to check if they lend Macbooks for a semester.&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#i-recommend-using-a-macbook-or-an-apple-computer-for-this-course-you-do-not-need-an-iphoneipad-for-this-course-if-you-do-not-have-a-macbook-you-can-try-macincloud-or-even-try-borrowing-macbooks-from-the-library-i-am-not-sure-how-long-you-can-borrow-a-computer-from-there-you-can-even-talk-to-khoury-systems-to-check-if-they-lend-macbooks-for-a-semester"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3 id="macincloud-could-be-unstable-for-you-if-you-do-not-have-a-reliable-internet-connection-so-try-it-they-give-you-a-day-for-099-as-soon-as-you-register-for-the-course-if-it-works-for-you-continue-this-course-or-else-talk-to-me"&gt;&lt;mark style="color:red;"&gt;MacInCloud could be unstable for you if you do not have a reliable Internet connection. So try it (they give you a day for $0.99) as soon as you register for the course. If it works for you, continue this course, or else talk to me&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;mark style="color:blue;"&gt;.&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#macincloud-could-be-unstable-for-you-if-you-do-not-have-a-reliable-internet-connection-so-try-it-they-give-you-a-day-for-099-as-soon-as-you-register-for-the-course-if-it-works-for-you-continue-this-course-or-else-talk-to-me"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are a Mac computer (Macbooks, iMacs, or Mac Pros) user, jump directly to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="setting-up-xcode.md" title="mention"&gt;setting-up-xcode.md&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>/docs/01-getting-started/getting-started/setting-up-xcode/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/docs/01-getting-started/getting-started/setting-up-xcode/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="setting-up-xcode"&gt;Setting up Xcode&lt;a class="anchor" href="#setting-up-xcode"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Setting up Xcode is also very simple. Let&amp;rsquo;s open Safari (or any browser you use) and type in &lt;a href="https://developer.apple.com/xcode/"&gt;https://developer.apple.com/xcode/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src="/gitbook-assets/Screenshot 2025-09-01 at 11.19.55 AM.png" alt=""&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Click on Download (on the top right) -&amp;gt; Mac App Store&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It opens up the AppStore application on your Mac. Sign in to your iCloud account. And click on the Download icon. Download Xcode 15, not beta. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src="/gitbook-assets/Screenshot 2023-05-06 at 11.47.42 AM (1).png" alt=""&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s wait until it downloads and installs Xcode.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>